today we're talking about some exciting  new game announcements and updates  including a big one for gotham knights  sony's march state of play is in the  books and with it came some new  announcements as well as some updates on  games that we already knew about the  announcement category features titles  like exo primal a new game from capcom  that puts you in a technologically  advanced mechanized battle suit so you  can handle fighting what seems like  thousands of extra dimensional dinosaurs  as they literally pour out of the sky  into human cities  others include valkyrie elysium deofield  or dial field chronicle and tmnt the  cowabunga collection  as for updates returnal is getting a new  survival mode and campaign co-op as part  of a free update  this is a feature that may convince me  to finally try out the game because i'll  finally have help for spoken was given a  new gameplay trailer despite the recent  delay from may to october and stranger  of paradise final fantasy origin is  getting a demo this demo's official  reveal follows a leak that suggested it  was on the way and now ps4 and ps5  players can grab the demo today and try  out the game before it's released on  march 18th however there was no word on  whether it will also arrive on xbox or  pc this demo will allow players to go  through the first three stages ending at  the western keep multiplayer is  supported and notably save data can be  carried over to the full game letting  you get a head start on the experience  to come unfortunately though there was  no new information about the sequel to  final fantasy 7 remake or final fantasy  16.  and sticking with final fantasy news to  celebrate the 35th anniversary of the  series a brand new website has been  launched which seems to be teasing  details about unannounced projects when  arriving on the website a piece of  anniversary artwork is front and center  featuring the warrior of light while the  iconic main theme song is played in the  background on the main page a message  simply states that the first final  fantasy title was released on december  18  1987 with 2022 making the 35th  anniversary of the series while also  teasing something new for fans the  message reads quote in this 35th  anniversary year we will be bringing you  many new exciting ways to enjoy the  worlds of final fantasy please look  forward to what final fantasy has in  store  switching gears to another exciting  announcement gotham knights developer  warner bros montreal has a new release  date for its upcoming action game  starring batman's vigilante family as  the game will now be released on october  25th of this year originally scheduled  to launch at the end of 2021 gotham  knights was delayed due to a need for  additional development time gotham  knights takes place in a world where  bruce wayne is very much dead leaving  gotham vulnerable to various criminal  gangs super villains and owl themed  secret societies that the dark knight  had once kept in check fortunately his  proteges nightwing batgirl robin and red  hood have stepped in to protect the city  and while that game was busy gaining a  release date advance wars was  unfortunately losing one advance wars  oneplus 2 rebootcamp which had been  scheduled to launch on the nintendo  switch in early april has been delayed  nintendo announced the news in a brief  tweet this morning attributing the move  to quote recent world events no doubt in  reference to russia's ongoing invasion  of ukraine  rebootcamp is a remake of the first two  advanced wars games for game boy advance  and it features the campaigns from both  along with the versus mode for playing  against ai or online  let us know in the comments what you're  hoping for in a future state of play and  what you hope comes of the 35th  anniversary year for final fantasy  [Applause]  [Music]  foreign
 

